  "projects": {
    "2016": [
      {
        "title": "Eventhooks for Discourse",
        "short_description": "I will build webhooks for Discourse. The webhook is a HTTP callback. It post the payload to external URL when an event happened.\nTechnical...",
        "description": "<p>I will build webhooks for Discourse. The webhook is a HTTP callback. It post the payload to external URL when an event happened.</p>\n<p>Technical considerations are available <a href=\"https://meta.discourse.org/t/gsoc-webhooks-proposal-draft/41468\" target=\"_blank\">on Discourse Meta</a>.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Erick Guan",
        "code_url": "https://meta.discourse.org/t/webhooks-feedback/49046",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2016/projects/6577775968256000/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Topic summaries, Canned Replies and Presence features",
        "short_description": "Some topics, like a call-for-bug-reports or a new Howto, will receive a lot of replies that go stale shortly thereafter because the appropriate...",
        "description": "<ol>\n<li><p>Some topics, like a call-for-bug-reports or a new Howto, will receive a lot of replies that go stale shortly thereafter because the appropriate fixes/edits were applied as a response. When closing or marking as solved doesn't make sense, the best solution to date is to delete these replies. Topic summaries offer a less destructive solution.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>A simple way for moderators to insert pre-written responses to common inquiries. Reduces repetitive actions, especially in support-centric communities.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>See who - apart from yourself - is using the \"Reply\" dialog box to write a reply to a particular topic. Targeted primarily at private group messages.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "student_name": "André Pereira",
        "code_url": "https://gist.github.com/adrapereira/f198238afb874ee692da08f4982aa203",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2016/projects/5975621553356800/"
      }
    ],
    "2017": [
      {
        "title": "Common Event System for Chatrooms",
        "short_description": "In our increasingly connected world, full of social media and internet-connected devices, it is important for systems to be interlinked to provide...",
        "description": "<p>In our increasingly connected world, full of social media and internet-connected devices, it is important for systems to be interlinked to provide the best user experience. Providing links between Discourse’s ‘long format’ discussion and instant-messaging applications is a natural way to promote real-time engagement with users. The discourse-slack plugin implements this well, and extending this functionality to more providers can only increase user engagement. This needs to be done in a maintainable way and creating a ‘common event system’ for chatroom plugins is the best way to do this.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "David Taylor",
        "code_url": "https://dtaylor.uk/blog/2017/08/gsoc_with_discourse/",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2017/projects/6383927988060160/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Advanced search enhancements & Autospec gem",
        "short_description": "The project proposes new filters to advanced search and extraction of the rake task for running unit tests into a separate gem. Advanced search...",
        "description": "<p>The project proposes new filters to advanced search and extraction of the rake task for running unit tests into a separate gem. Advanced search enhancements contains 1) searching posts containing all of the entered tags and 2) searching posts with images (with extension for searching by any filetype). The benefit for the Discourse community is better filtering of posts with emphasis on the search performance which will be useful for searching in bigger forums. By extracting custom way of running unit tests into a gem, we separate concerns as the tests running library is not dependent on the Discourse, Discourse code base gets smaller and it will be beneficial to whole Rails community.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Jakub Macina",
        "code_url": "https://gist.github.com/dmacjam/66211e9149ad72537bc12d0e483ea9e1",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2017/projects/5545567551750144/"
      },
      {
        "title": "General improvements to Discourse",
        "short_description": "This project is meant to improve the core of Discourse and implement new plugins. The features that are going to be implemented are:\n\nPLUGIN: Convert...",
        "description": "<p>This project is meant to improve the core of Discourse and implement new plugins. The features that are going to be implemented are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>PLUGIN: Convert GIFs to MP4/WebP</li>\n<li>CORE: General improvements to user’s profile and SSO</li>\n<li>PLUGIN: Topic list tabs for user-customizeable saved filters\nAs a stretch goal, I decided to work on:</li>\n<li>CORE: Tracking signups from referral</li>\n<li>PLUGIN: Passwordless signin via email link</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These features should improve considerably users' experience and make it an even better forum software.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Bianca Nenciu",
        "code_url": "https://github.com/nbianca/gsoc-2017",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2017/projects/5584241047896064/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Unicode username and search improvements",
        "short_description": "I will improve Unicode/i18n for Discourse, especially a Unicode username feature.\nThis includes a new gem to leverage on battle-tested ICU library...",
        "description": "<p>I will improve Unicode/i18n for Discourse, especially a Unicode username feature.\nThis includes a new gem to leverage on battle-tested ICU library and a so called \\emph{i18n backend}.\nThe Unicode/i18n problem has already being handled by Rails but there are also limitation without improvement\nover years. Leveraging on Rails is not enough.</p>\n<p>I'll also improve the CJK search. That includes a set of plugins for PostgreSQL so that the index quality\ncan be further improved. Along with the refactors with search module, Discourse search for CJK forum should\nbe improved.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Erick Guan",
        "code_url": "https://github.com/discourse/discourse/pulls?utf8=%E2%9C%93&q=is%3Apr%20author%3Afantasticfears%20",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2017/projects/5173734516195328/"
      }
    ]
  },
